# 3. PLATFORM AND DEVELOPMENT SCOPE

## Phase 1: Android mobile application

Build and test the Android application first.

Requirements:

- Mobile-first layouts.
- Responsive screens for different Android screen sizes.
- Touch-friendly controls.
- Support for Android back navigation.
- Keyboard-safe chat and editor layouts.
- Proper loading, empty, success, and error states.
- Local project persistence.
- Google sign-in using Firebase Authentication.
- Optional synchronization of selected project information.
- Secure AI integration.
- A buildable Android project with reproducible APK instructions.

The application must not depend on owning a public domain simply to install or use the app.

**Important implementation rule:** Select a technology that can genuinely produce an Android APK. If the available Google AI Studio environment cannot compile a native Android project, generate the complete source repository and provide a verified Android Studio build workflow. Do not pretend a web preview is an installed Android app.

## Phase 2: Windows desktop application

This phase is outside the initial implementation.

When requested, develop a separate Windows application with its own interface and packaging process. Reuse suitable backend APIs and shared business logic where practical, but do not force the mobile interface into a desktop layout.

Deliver a Windows EXE only after the Windows build has actually succeeded.

