# 21. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES

## Phase 1 — Foundation

Implement the project structure, navigation, local persistence, dependency configuration, error handling, and test infrastructure.

**Deliverable:** A buildable Android foundation with persistent local state.

## Phase 2 — Authentication and data

Implement Google sign-in, Firebase Authentication, secure data rules, and optional synchronization.

**Deliverable:** A working account and recovery flow.

## Phase 3 — Chat and AI

Implement text input, requirement analysis, structured planning, and secure AI service communication.

**Deliverable:** A working conversational workflow.

## Phase 4 — Website generation

Implement project generation, file management, editing, versioning, and validation.

**Deliverable:** A generated website project with real source files.

## Phase 5 — Testing and preview

Implement the test pipeline, error recovery, and supported preview functionality.

**Deliverable:** A project that can be inspected and tested.

## Phase 6 — Export and deployment

Implement safe source-code export and a real hosting-provider integration.

**Deliverable:** A verified export and, once configured, a verified live URL.

## Phase 7 — Quality assurance

Run the acceptance tests, review security, assess performance, fix defects, and document limitations.

**Deliverable:** A release candidate and a transparent test report.

Do not mark a phase complete merely because its interface has been generated.

